From e8babbe4dd3893c645a1b3905d6b231a04e1dc91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Mar 2026 14:24:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add min_change miner power allocation strategy

New strategy that minimizes the number of miner setpoint changes when
adjusting total power. Instead of recalculating all targets from scratch
(proportional), it applies the delta to the fewest miners possible:

- For increases: fills active miners with most headroom first, wakes
  sleeping miners only if needed
- For decreases: tries single-miner reduction first, then sleeps
  smallest miners and reduces next
- Maintains phase balance (equal split across A/B/C)
- Skips unchanged miners entirely (no API call sent)

Config: SupervisorConfig.miner_power_strategy = 'min_change' | 'proportional'
Default remains 'proportional' for backward compatibility.

28 new tests (22 unit + 6 Ray integration), zero regressions.

https://claude.ai/code/session_01H6YkrU2kDQgqbZoE2WHB1Y
